#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:85
#: bca76ed5f6c9480c881c62a5bf1e5cd1
msgid "\"Cannot connect to qrexec agent\" error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:88
#: 5783d5f4dd1f402c8843effce3c936e0
msgid ""
"If you face this error when starting a VM, look into the VM logs at ``/var/"
"log/xen/console/guest-VMNAME.log``. Common reasons that may be revealed are: "
"too low memory, corrupted files or a VM crash on startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:90
#: 996555f3e2244943a02adad9e9d72420
msgid ""
"If the error occurs as a result of too little initial memory, increase the "
"initial memory from 200MB to 400MB by navigating to VM settings » Advanced » "
"Initial memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:93
#: be225da521a1443f801c4848afb367e9
msgid "\"No match found\" when trying to install a template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:96
#: c6109b51d3a34187af0fc2ffb4c5243a
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:106
#: 7cf67d2ce53e40b09fab5ad5759c00a9
msgid ""
"This normally means you already have the template installed. It may be that "
"you have the matching package installed, but you removed or renamed the "
"template. Check ``rpm -q qubes-template-<name>``. If it lists the package, "
"but you don’t really have the template present (``qvm-ls`` doesn’t list it), "
"you need to clean up leftovers of the package with ``rpm -e --noscripts "
"qubes-template-<name>``, then install it normally."
msgstr ""
